@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;security] peach-projection-authority
Peach MUST obtain each reflection projection through Marshall's dedicated Peach
control service. Peach MUST NOT read Marshall PostgreSQL directly, derive VM or
integration authority from guest-supplied identity fields, or serve a retained
snapshot after control admission fails.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] peach-local-binding-and-secret-boundary
An HTTP reflection response MUST require a validated private-service binding for
Peach's configured host and a protocol-valid Marshall snapshot. Responses MUST
omit credentials, integration header values and control tokens. Unknown paths,
malformed bindings and failed control requests MUST NOT return a projection.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;deployment] peach-dedicated-control-custody
Peach MUST use its dedicated host-bound control credential and configured CA.
Compute or Audi credentials MUST NOT authenticate Peach requests. Credentials and
reflection request payloads MUST NOT enter diagnostic output or the Nix store.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] peach-evidence-boundary
Projection codec fixtures MUST NOT be represented as HTTP, native guest, network
isolation, credential lifecycle or production deployment acceptance. Such claims
MUST identify the exact executed test and supporting result.
